architecture web-route-table
  source_lineage earliest source cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c first committed 2026-11-05 in 44c1481e "feat: land Aug 24 - Nov 5 native estate work"
  canonical_name WebRouteTable
  family forwarding
  domain Forwarding / HTTP Route Declaration
  layer forwarding
  semantic_question Which native owner is asked about a public path, under which request facts, and in what order, without a hand-written branch per page in the WebAddress request loop?
  purpose Declares every WebAddress route owner once in CUE as an ordered row (owner, exact, strict, prefix, any, records or semantic match, a path, optional request facts, an optional name for the path, an optional plain-words title) and compiles it into a static table that one dispatcher walks. Owners take one BfRequest and test the declared name of the path they were asked about, so a path is spelled in one place. A records row's paths are rows of a store declared in schemas/storage/stores (the first: published CMS notes, wiki_page rows under /notes/), so a new page is a record and answers without a rebuild. The table ends in one semantic row: when the resolver finds nothing at an HTML address, the 404 page offers up to five titled rows and guest-readable records nearest the missing path, ranked by the higher of the distilled static embedding cosine and a character-trigram overlap.
  maturity implemented
  source_path schemas/control/web-routes.cue
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tools/compile_web_routes.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/web_request.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/generated/native_web_routes.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/main.c
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/web_route_kinds.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/src/surface_fragments_and_ops.h
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_route_kinds_test.sh
  source_path cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/Makefile
  source_path scripts/ui-ratchet.sh
  invariant the CUE list order is the dispatch order; the first owner that answers ends the request, and an owner already asked for a request is not asked again
  invariant a row's when facts (get, site_root, html, not_json, json, not_territory_apex) are computed once per request from the method, Accept, Host and server root; an owner is asked only when every fact its row names holds
  invariant an owner asked through a row sees that row's declared name in BfRequest.as; a caller that picks an owner directly (the static export, the public asset export) asks it through the owner's own first matching row so it sees the same name
  invariant the table ends in rows that always answer (the resolver, then a transport-level 405 for any non-GET), so nothing falls past dispatch
  invariant owners still check their own method, origin, session and authority; the table only decides who is asked
  invariant main.c holds one dispatch call and no per-owner branch; the ui-ratchet dispatch_branches and route_path_compares counts may only go down
  invariant a records row asks its store only after its prefix matched, read-only through the store's declared durability and request lease (cms_open_ro for the cms store), with a declared SELECT that tests exactly what the owner tests; the compiler refuses a store not declared as opened by cmd/BonfyreWebAddress, and a statement that would write is refused at run time
  invariant a records row sits in its owner's old place in the order and adds no when fact; the owner keeps its method, session and guest checks (a published note that is not guest-readable still answers 401 from the owner)
  invariant the semantic row is exactly one and last; it never matches a request, and only the resolver's HTML not-found branch reads it; machine representations keep the resolver's JSON verdict byte for byte
  invariant a suggestion is offered only from a titled row whose when facts hold for a browser GET on this host and server, or from a record set's declared suggest query that applies the owner's own index rule (published and guest-readable); the status stays 404
  forbidden_inference a suggestion -> the route exists for this caller, the caller may open it, or the owner will answer
  forbidden_inference a high suggestion score -> the same meaning; the static vector has no word order and scores compare only within one .bfse
  forbidden_inference a records match -> the owner will answer 200 or that the record is readable by this caller
  forbidden_inference a declared route -> the request is authorized, the caller is signed in, the method is allowed, or the owner will answer
  forbidden_inference a row's when facts -> content negotiation is complete or the representation the owner returns
  forbidden_inference a row's declared name (as) -> a capability, scope or grant; it is a label for a path, never an authority token
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/web_route_kinds_test.sh (make web-route-kinds-witness): a running server 404s /notes/river-crossing, answers 200 the moment the wiki_page row is inserted with no rebuild or restart, keeps the owner's 401 for a non-guest note and 404 for a draft, ranks the record first for /notes/river-crosing, offers /communities for /comunities and /what-things-cost for /prices, shows the empty state for /zqxjv, never offers non-guest or draft records, and keeps the JSON not_found verdict for machines
  witness 2026-11-15 comparison of 1,720 requests (every declared path, path+x and path+/ plus 29 tail paths; GET and POST; text/html and application/json) against a binary built from HEAD on cloned stores: 0 status or redirect differences, 1,539 identical bodies, 177 differing bodies all GET text/html 404s, and 4 /ops bodies that vary between repeated requests on HEAD itself
  witness cmd/BonfyreWebAddress/tests/native_surface_routes_test.sh, account_continuity_test.sh, work_orders_test.sh, guild_household_records_test.sh, detail_depth_test.sh and participant_journey_browser.test.mjs drive owners through the compiled table on a running server
  witness 2026-11-16 comparison of 283 requests (every declared path plus the paths of each converted any row, GET and POST) between a binary built before and after 46 any rows became declared rows: 0 status or redirect differences except /x (a fact-surface row added by another lane meanwhile); differing bodies are per-request nonces (/organizations), /ops, pages other lanes re-marked (/sources, /link), and 404 suggestion lists
  forbidden_inference a declared path row for an owner that once sat on an any row -> the owner answers every request on that path; it still checks its method, host, session and sub-path
  known_gap 25 any rows remain: host-scoped owners (site MCP, delegated private hosts, the Observatory), owners whose paths are data (site programs, authored pages, donor routes, the machine web and IndexNow key, spatial frontier, flows, market fronts, protocols, packs, human community, external candidates, auth) and the resolver tail; each needs a records row or a declared path family before it can leave any
  known_gap only one record set exists (CMS notes); member addresses (/people/<person>) stay a prefix row because that owner answers its own 404 and redirect, and route_presentation rows are presentation only (their owner keeps the route), so neither is a route source yet
  known_gap the ranker is the static model blended with trigrams; the BitNet address ranker is SHADOW-only on ARM and is not used here, and suggestion quality is measured only by the witness cases, not by a labelled set of missed paths
  known_gap other owners' own 404s (an owner that answers 404 itself) do not reach the resolver tail and show no suggestions
  known_gap the static_asset_closure_test fixture answers bf_web_route_ask by calling the owner directly, so it does not exercise the row lookup
